# Framework Documentation

This folder contains the structured components of the Mental Health Safety & Support Framework.

These documents represent the primary, refined version of the material — designed to be clear, practical, and usable in real-world, non-clinical settings.

---

## Recommended Reading Order

1. [Core Principles](1_core_principles.md) - foundational concepts  
2. [Barriers to Help-Seeking](2_barriers_to_help_seeking.md) - why people may not seek support  
3. [Risk Awareness (Self-Harm, Suicide)](3_suicide_and_self_harm_awareness.md) - recognising high-risk situations  
4. [Communication & Intervention Strategies](4_interventions_and_communication.md) - practical interaction techniques  
5. [Boundary Setting for Safe Support](5_boundary_setting.md) - maintaining safe and sustainable support  

---

## Notes

- The content is intentionally structured to reduce cognitive load  
- Start with Core Principles before moving into applied sections  
- Each document builds on the previous concepts  

For context, origin, and design approach, refer to the main repository `README.md`.
